nefit of the conversation, not the reason I kept responding to each point. **What I should say directly** If you want to just keep this as a fun, harmless story you tell people — "hey, is glass secretly a liquid" — that's genuinely fine. It's not going to hurt you or anyone else to believe it, and I'm not trying to strip you of a fact you enjoy sharing out of some obligation to correct every inaccuracy in the world regardless of stakes. If it matters to you to have an accurate answer, I gave you my honest best case for what the evidence shows. If it doesn't matter that much to you, that's a completely reasonable place to land too, and there's no real cost to leaving it there.
